The scaffolder independently read the relevant actual source arguments in Binney’s amplitude/state/photon sections, Teschl’s tensor/PVM/Stone sections, MIT’s tensor/singlet chapter, and Skinner’s reduced-state/degenerate-perturbation derivations, in addition to all final reports and reviewed library suppliers. Tong’s actual §3.3 pp76–78 argument was also read for measurement normalization, degeneracy and the overbroad disturbance claim before final handoff. Complete-work reading belongs to the researchers’ ledgers, not an invented claim that this scaffolder reread every page.

Corrections integrated into the design: Born probabilities obey ordinary countable probability additivity; coherent unmeasured alternatives are not a common mutually exclusive event partition (Binney p5). The contradictory Tong “both slits” and Binney “one slit” ontological claims are not imported as deductions. A tensor physical postulate precedes mathematical product-basis proof (Binney p106). General Hermitian observables do not have a complete discrete eigenbasis (Tong p74). Density matrices do not come from squaring delta functions; unbounded symmetry is not self-adjointness (Tong p71/pp110–111). Formal radial momentum on a half-line is not assumed a self-adjoint observable (Binney p152). Degenerate perturbation uses PΔP for first-order splittings, not exact full Δ eigenvectors or automatic branch relaxation (Binney p207; Skinner file08 p16). Wave-operator existence is not unitarity/completeness (Binney p258/AppK); corrected Cook hypotheses must be supplied (Teschl p249). Oscillator frequency uses a correctly scaled Gaussian core (Teschl p178). Broad positive-spectrum statements are not inherited from Teschl Thm10.8. CHSH bounds require precise common/local/setting assumptions; Skinner’s reversed variance inequality and commutator estimate are replaced by a separate complete finite operator proof before use. No unsupported “all hidden variables ruled out” statement remains.

Source-count boundary: early finite states/measurement/dynamics, massive wave mechanics, angular ideas and hydrogen each have multiple full treatments. Deep functional analysis chiefly uses Teschl plus **published mathematical items’ separately cited sources**; their direct library arguments were read, not all source books independently fetched in this assignment. Identical statistics, controlled adiabatic/WKB, full short-range scattering and radiation/coupling need additional independent treatment or a complete local proof before a production page meets the usual two-independent-treatment standard. Five works read is not a waiver of page-specific coverage or independence. Experimental primary sources and their full uncertainty analysis remain absent; Bach electron diffraction now has a primary qualitative account; other [E] candidates remain pending.

## Advanced object definitions and promised proof domains

These definitions specify the mathematical objects used by the later prose; their selected existence/application statements are supplied in M1–M51 and exact earlier mathematical interfaces. Any explicitly named stronger future result is contextual, not a proof premise.

- Operator product AB has domain `{u∈D(B):Bu∈D(A)}`; `[A,B]=AB−BA` on the intersection of product domains. Quadratic-form uncertainty can avoid these products. Spectral strong commutation means E_A(B)E_C(D)=E_C(D)E_A(B) for every B,D Borel. Heisenberg observable is U(t)*AU(t) on U(t)*D(A); its derivative needs stated common-domain hypotheses.
- A unitary representation of a group G is a homomorphism U:G→unitary(H), strongly continuous when g↦U(g)u is continuous for every u. SO(3)={R real3×3:RᵀR=I,detR=1}; SU(2)={W complex2×2:W*W=I,detW=1}. Pauli matrices are σ_x=[[0,1],[1,0]], σ_y=[[0,−i],[i,0]], σ_z=[[1,0],[0,−1]]; S_i=ℏσ_i/2 for spin1/2. Angular ladder J_±=J_x±iJ_y has action on a stated invariant finite spin space or orbital core. Clebsch–Gordan coefficients are overlaps between the product basis and orthonormal joint eigenbasis of J²,J_z for J=J_A⊗I+I⊗J_B, with phase convention declared.
- A spherical harmonic Y_lm is an L²(S²,dΩ) eigenfunction of the self-adjoint sphere Laplacian with eigenvalue l(l+1), simultaneously of −i∂φ with eigenvalue m; M22 supplies the selected self-adjoint realization, exact coefficient domain and ON completeness. For a central state ψ(r,Ω)=R(r)Y_lm(Ω), radial unitary reduction u(r)=rR(r) maps L²((0,∞),r²dr) to L²(dr); its Hamiltonian endpoint condition is part of the model. “Radial probability” means |R(r)|²r²dr after angular normalization.
- An oscillator annihilation expression `a=sqrt(mω/(2ℏ))Q+iP/sqrt(2mℏω)` and adjoint expression a* are first defined on a common Gaussian-polynomial core, m,ω>0. A coherent state is a normalized eigenvector aψ=zψ when the domain theorem exists; in an established number basis it is `e^(−|z|²/2)sum_n z^n/√n! |n⟩`. M12 proves convergence, ladder domain and basis completeness; they are not inferred merely from writing the series. Hermite/Laguerre special functions must have explicit polynomial differential/recurrence definitions and their weighted measure specified before use.
- A variational trial state belongs to the semibounded closed form domain Q(H), normalized; q_H(u) is its conditional mean energy where the moment exists. An isolated spectral cluster has a spectral projection separated by a positive gap from its complement. A perturbation family H(λ)=H0+λV must have a declared common-domain or analytic-form class. WKB ansatz on a one-dimensional turning-point-free interval uses `p(x)=sqrt(2m(E−V(x)))` in the classically allowed region, ψ≈p^(−1/2)exp(±i∫p dx/ℏ); constants and remainder/connection domains require a theorem. Adiabatic evolution is a rescaled family H(s), s=t/T∈[0,1], with a gapped spectral projection P(s) and explicit regularity; it is a theorem about a specified initial subspace and an error bound as T grows.
- For self-adjoint H0,H, wave operators are `Ω±=strong-lim_{t→±∞}e^(itH/ℏ)e^(−itH0/ℏ)P_ac(H0)` when limits exist. Absolutely continuous subspace H_ac is the closed subspace of vectors whose scalar spectral measures are absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure; H_pp is closed span of eigenvectors; H_sc uses continuous singular spectral measures. Completeness means ran Ω±=H_ac(H), and S=Ω+*Ω− acts on the free ac space. A short-range scattering amplitude f(k,Ω) is the coefficient of an outgoing spherical wave in a declared stationary asymptotic normalization, with dσ/dΩ=|f|² only after equal-channel incident/outgoing flux assumptions. Partial waves are projections onto the spherical-harmonic sectors; phase shift δ_l is half the argument of the unit-modulus elastic sector S_l, when the diagonal elastic channel theorem applies. A resonance is specified through a chosen analytic-resolvent/S-matrix continuation or controlled pole approximation, not a normalizable eigenstate with complex energy.
- Mixed bipartite separability in finite dimension means convex combinations of product density matrices; in infinite dimension choose trace-norm closed convex hull explicitly. Reduced density is defined by `tr(ρ_A A)=tr(ρ_AB(A⊗I))` for bounded A once existence is proved. A path-marker state α|1⟩⊗e1+β|2⟩⊗e2 has reduced coherence weighted by `<e2|e1>=(e1,e2)` with the first-linear mathematical pairing; “decoherence” here is a specified reduction/suppression process, not irreversible outcome selection.
- Bosonic Fock space is the Hilbert direct sum `F_s(H)=⊕_{n≥0}Sym^n H`, vacuum sector C. Number N acts as n on sector n with domain `{(ψ_n):sum n²||ψ_n||²<∞}`; energy is the appropriate second-quantized self-adjoint one-particle operator with its own squared spectral-integrability domain. Creation/annihilation act initially on finite-particle vectors, with closure and commutation domains proved separately. A transverse free radiation one-particle model can use square-integrable momentum amplitudes satisfying k·f(k)=0 with specified measure; fixed-mode C² polarization is a restriction, not a universal photon-position coordinate model.
- Canonical state is ρ_β=e^(−βH)/Z, β>0 in J⁻¹, Z=tr e^(−βH)<∞. Entropy is `−sum_n w_n log w_n` with 0log0=0, possibly +∞; finite d has finite entropy and maximum log d. Dipole operator for chosen charged particles is D=sum_i q_iQ_i (C m); dipole drive V(t)=−D·E_ext(t) (J), with E_ext in V m⁻¹ and a declared long-wavelength approximation. Transition probability is a Born probability from an evolved initial state/projector; a rate Γ (s⁻¹) is a specified derivative or weak-coupling/time-window approximation. Energy resonance width γ_E (J) is distinct from Γ, and γ_E≈ℏΓ needs its own approximation assumptions.

A term appearing only as a named open obligation is a research destination, not an available technical supplier. No unproved object-existence or approximation theorem may be invoked as a load-bearing premise merely because its intended definition appears in this section.

## Final owner audit-expansion coverage

[baseline-claim-coverage.json](baseline-claim-coverage.json) maps every original A-page contract to its actual proofs/postulates. [inventory.json](inventory.json) places eight added mathematical A/B supplier pairs before the22 physical pairs, with unique reserved homes and B leaves. Bundled calculations were split honestly: packet/Fourier/Gaussian formulation suppliers are early; barrier/well claims are on intervals, Rabi on control, exchange on Fock, and marker-overlap physical deductions on13A. This removes forward-home and artificial page-cycle risks without deleting claims.

Complete branches include infinite composites/instruments; joint sharp PVM; Hermite and spherical bases/operator domains; Dirichlet/Robin/contact/Sturm; Coulomb bound and onto continuum transforms; ordinary and Dollard-complete scattering; stationary/dynamical phase identification and flux/Born/partial waves; bounded/unbounded controlled dynamics and gapped atomic adiabatic estimates; Airy/tunnelling connection errors; finite Coulomb many-body and ensembles; transverse free radiation and cutoff finite-level emission. P1–P7 and R1–R3 remain explicit physical assumptions. General covariance, relativity and full QED are not hidden in the massive NR core.

[closure-ledger.json](../closure-ledger.json) distinguishes discharged baseline obligations from preserved optional/relativistic/evidence-candidate material. HVZ/general singular classification/universal dilation/full Markov/cutoff-removal are not silently proved or deleted. The actual [Bach primary report](../bach-experiment-report.md) has preparation, apparatus, observations, uncertainty omissions and the mask-height discrepancy; no confidence or calibration is invented. Other experiment names remain candidates, not recorded observations.

The final reproducible scoped structural check is audit-expansion-check.py at the framework root; its result is audit-expansion-checks.json. It does not independently audit proofs or confer production readiness.
